// Card CG10-INDIRECT-ACCESS-SOLE-RESIDUALS (wave 48, round 18): the three
// value operations of `cmt_atomic`, which W37 left undeclared above
// (`CMT-ATOMIC-BACKEND-COPIES`). Each is the NEUTRAL ELEMENT (every formal
// borrowed, the scalar result `resource_return_none()`), pinned (contract
// spec C06.2) after reading every definition at both audited revisions
// (`66910c10` and `046accf6`: `cmt_atomic.h` and the four backend files are
// byte-identical across the two).
//
// ## Why the backend copies do not decline these
//
// The W37 refinement of `ADD-NAME-COLLISION`: what matters is whether the
// definitions AGREE, not how many there are. CMake compiles exactly one
// backend (`src/CMakeLists.txt`: `cmt_atomic_msvc.c`, `_clang.c`, `_gcc.c` or
// `_generic.c`); all five definitions of each name spell the prototype of
// `include/cmetrics/cmt_atomic.h:7-9` and agree on custody:
//
//   * `_gcc.c` and `_clang.c` (byte-identical bodies): `__atomic_load_n`,
//     `__atomic_store_n`, `__atomic_compare_exchange` on `storage`;
//   * `_generic.c`: the same reads and writes of `*storage` under a global
//     `pthread_mutex_t` set up once by `pthread_once`, returning 0 when that
//     set-up failed;
//   * `_msvc.c`: under a global `CRITICAL_SECTION` (32-bit) or with
//     `_Interlocked*64` intrinsics (`_WIN64`).
//
// Every definition reads and/or writes the `uint64_t` at `storage` and returns
// a scalar (`int`, `void`, `uint64_t`). None frees, stores, retains or
// transfers `storage`, and no custody crosses the call in either direction.
// `cmt_atomic_clang.c` is the unit the corpus analyses (its `cmt_atomic_*`
// rows are `Safe` on the BEFORE run), so
// constraint 8's duty gate compares these declarations with the W4 summary
// of that body there.
//
// ## Why now
//
// Gateway rule 12k names `cmt_atomic_load`/`_store`/`_compare_exchange` as
// what decides refused statements (`cmt_atomic_load(&metric->hist_count)`)
// of the functions the indirect-access refusal blocked alone, 19 of them by
// one of these three callees alone. The calls sit in other units, which no
// summary route reaches.
//
// ## ABI (constraint 8)
//
// `uint64_t *` is `ptr<mut, u8>`; `uint64_t` is `u64`, `int` `i32`, `void`
// `unit` (LP64).
//
// NOT CLAIMED: atomicity, memory ordering, the generic backend's 0 on a
// failed mutex set-up, or `storage`'s validity or lifetime.

// --- read a 64-bit value atomically ---
extern fn cmt_atomic_load(storage: ptr<mut, u8>) -> u64
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(storage);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// --- store a 64-bit value atomically ---
extern fn cmt_atomic_store(storage: ptr<mut, u8>, new_value: u64) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(storage);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(new_value);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// --- compare and exchange a 64-bit value atomically ---
extern fn cmt_atomic_compare_exchange(storage: ptr<mut, u8>, old_value: u64, new_value: u64) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(storage);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(old_value);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(new_value);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
